# Expected SHA-256 digests of the published ai-specs release assets (v0.25.0).
# This file is the trust root (D5): the network supplies only bytes, the
# repository supplies the expected digest. A downloaded asset whose SHA-256 does
# not match is deleted and never installed: install.sh and `ai-specs upgrade`
# verify it BEFORE replacing anything.
#
# Reproduce any digest locally with:
#   scripts/build-cli.sh
#   cd dist && shasum -a 256 ai-specs-darwin-amd64 ai-specs-darwin-arm64 \
#     ai-specs-linux-amd64 ai-specs-linux-arm64
#
# CANONICAL TOOLCHAIN: Go builds are deterministic for a given toolchain, but
# different Go releases compile different stdlib bytes. These digests were
# generated with go1.24.13 — the same version the release CI pins
# (.github/workflows/release-binaries.yml) — and MUST be regenerated with
# exactly that version, or the CI checksum gate fails the release.
#
# EMBEDDED ASSETS ARE PART OF THESE DIGESTS: the binary carries the catalog/,
# templates/, bundled-skills/ and bundled-commands/ trees (card [Go 06]), so a
# change anywhere inside them — a comment in an embedded file included — changes
# the binary bytes. Regenerate this file in the SAME commit as any such change,
# or the installer will refuse the published asset as a mismatch (correctly).
#
# The four executable assets are intentionally CI/release outputs, not tracked
# files. These lines are their source-level trust manifest; regenerate them with
# scripts/build-cli.sh after any CLI change and verify before publishing.
#
